## Multiple smooth terms

Streaming GAMs support the same formula syntax as regular GAMs:

::: {#6bde3ec9 .cell execution_count=12}
``` {.python .cell-code}
# Two smooth terms
rng = np.random.default_rng(42)
n = 300
x1 = np.linspace(0, 2 * np.pi, n)
x2 = rng.uniform(0, 1, n)
y = np.sin(x1) + 2 * x2 + rng.normal(0, 0.3, n)

sgam2 = wk.StreamingGAM("y ~ s(x1) + s(x2)")
batch_size = 100
for i in range(0, n, batch_size):
    batch = {"x1": x1[i:i + batch_size], "x2": x2[i:i + batch_size], "y": y[i:i + batch_size]}
    sgam2.partial_fit(batch)
sgam2.solve()

print(sgam2.summary())
```

